#!/bin/bash
# land-sand-and-plates.sh — the Beauty hub, redrawn from the owner's references.
#
#   1. BEAUTY GETS A GROUND. Warm sand page, cream cards, from the owner's
#      swatch photograph. The third ground grant in the city; the argument is
#      written into relief.spec, not asserted. Read it before touching it.
#   2. THE SKIN & HAIR PAGE IS BUILT FROM THE POSTER REFERENCE. Every section is
#      a printed plate — masthead rule, display-serif title, star divider,
#      tracked blurb, foot rule — and the plate IS the header of its fold.
#   3. AND IT FOLDS. Once there is an assessment, every section closes; one tap
#      opens any of them, and a closed header still says what is inside it.
#
# WEB APP ONLY (together-city-react). Vercel. No API change, no migration.
# PRECONDITION: land-hide-makeup.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A room the colour of what it sells"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"Off the menu is not deleted"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-hide-makeup.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="3f5205ef00ff0608f0832e7b7bba2a0379335daff49b0ddec054e812322d3e4c"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied"

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add -A together-city-react/src
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A room the colour of what it sells

THE BEAUTY HUB, REDRAWN FROM TWO REFERENCES THE OWNER SUPPLIED.

── THE GROUND: THE THIRD GRANT THE CITY HAS GIVEN ─────────────────────────────

Warm sand page, cream cards, sampled from the owner's swatch photograph.

The argument is in relief.spec beside the other five entries, and it is
deliberately NOT the argument social and dating made and lost. Those two asked
for a tint to hold photographs and were refused with: a wall of pictures on
white is a contact sheet, and a contact sheet is fixed by casing and space
rather than by colour. That refusal stands and relief.css enforces it.

It does not reach this hub, because the problem here is not density, it is
VALUE. Skincare is photographed cut-out — a white cream, an ivory balm, a
translucent gel. Those pictures are `.no-case` of necessity, since an outline
round a cut-out is an outline round nothing, and they are the same value as the
city's paper. A cased portrait on white loses its frame and gets it back from
the case; an uncased white cream on white loses the CREAM, and no amount of air
returns it.

The hue is not the ground: this is a neutral warm sand and beauty's magenta
appears nowhere below the rail lamp, where every hub's hue lives. It is a light
room, so the five depths are inherited untouched — the cheapest of the three
grants and the cleanest to hand back.

Every ink is measured against this hub's own ground by relief.spec at build
time, which is what a grant buys. Two failed at the root values and only two:
green at 4.36 and amber at 4.48, which sit close to sand in luminance where red
and blue do not. Both are the same hue taken down until they clear.

── THE PLATE: THE PAGE IS THE POSTER ──────────────────────────────────────────

The second reference is four editorial prints, all one object: SKIN · BEAUTY ·
CARE across the top, a display-serif title set large and centred, a
hairline–star–hairline divider, a paragraph in wide-tracked capitals, and a foot
rule. Every section of the skin & hair page is now one of those.

AND THE PLATE IS THE HEADER OF ITS FOLD rather than a lid sitting on one. That
is what keeps the page from becoming five posters with a real interface hidden
underneath: the poster IS the interface, and the working content opens out of
it. The affordance lives in the foot rule where the reference prints EST. 2024,
because there is nowhere on a centred composition for a chevron to go.

Three things are deliberately NOT plates. The parts of the assessment — Skin,
Hair & scalp, Ingredients, Good to know — are set as an INDEX, because they are
the contents of one chapter rather than four more chapters, and seven posters in
a column is the failure that makes a reference stop reading as a reference. A
budget that has never been set stays an open card, because a poster you have to
open first is a poster standing in front of the only unfinished step. And a
plate with nothing behind it renders as a heading rather than as a fold, because
a collapsed region controlling nothing is a heading that has been lied about.

Three smaller things went with the redesign. `.routine-display` is now
`.beauty-display`: it was named after the first page that needed the display
serif, and asking for a sixth grant called `.beauty-plate-title` would have been
asking permission to do what the existing grant already permits — one hub, one
display class, carrying the FACE and no size, so a new plate cannot resize a
masthead on another page. The plain rounded Collapsible is gone rather than left
as an unused third option. And the gendered emoji avatar left with the heading
it sat in; the rule it existed to keep — nothing in this hub is gated by gender —
is unchanged and written down where it was.

── AND EVERY SECTION FOLDS ONCE IT HAS AN ANSWER IN IT ────────────────────────

Seven skin readings, five hair readings and nine ingredients were three screens
of something already read, standing between somebody and the two things on the
page that change. Each closed header carries a summary, because a fold that says
only its own name gives nobody a reason to open it: "7 readings · 3 to work on"
is the reason to open, and "5 readings · all good" is a complete answer without
opening anything.

The gate is having an assessment, not having answered all eighteen questions.
Under the old gate, ADDING a question to the form would have re-opened the whole
page for everybody who had already finished it — a section is done when IT has
produced something. The photo section is the one exception and opens again while
photographs are staged, because switching tabs unmounts it and folding it away
with somebody's photos inside, one click from the Analyse button, is worse than
not folding at all.

Backend untouched: no route, no schema, no query changed.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A room the colour of what it sells
 Push — Vercel rebuilds. Open /beauty/profile: sand ground,
 cream plates, every section closed with its counts on the
 foot rule.
===============================================================

DONE
